{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794978509598584906,"compiled_state":{"alias":"powderblue-effectual-racerunner","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"cf1b6f75abced944852510cc1d907296a11f70472ad6906c3f5bc844a1d1b5fc","event_uuid":"f3b5ddb0-36d9-428f-9312-083db789b697","position":{"commit_sha":"a459a44d0b7c2391ad48ad7c00cd63b1aea4b6f8","position":"1794978491173823963-f3b5ddb0-36d9-428f-9312-083db789b697"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a2c8541fc51b025d93e1ce98495829206bc5f00377f65a5e0be3258ab0dbb0ca","event_uuid":"ce25c9a1-5015-43a8-b149-800bbcc88250","position":{"commit_sha":"aee92848e86b2d5a1f7d49095a72be189ea53fa2","position":"1794978509598584905-ce25c9a1-5015-43a8-b149-800bbcc88250"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794978491173823963,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ce25c9a1-5015-43a8-b149-800bbcc88250","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c691-bbc1-4217-4cf4"}],"description":"## Observation\nIn run 44232977541 at dd72b461814, the \"sweep (windows)\" job (134562252974) printed this from the crash guard's timeout banner:\n\n`+++ Timeout +++ pytest-timeout expired after 600.0s in tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py::test_write_survives_foreground_maintenance_repack (xdist worker gw3)`\n\nThe stack dump shows the test thread at `tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py:67` (`_fill_loose`), called from `_cross_the_maintenance_threshold` (`:184`). It is blocked in `subprocess.run(... communicate)` on `git -C <tracker> hash-object -w --stdin-paths`, while a separate thread is still in `subprocess._stdin_write` feeding the path list.\n\nThe same failure appears without a banner in run 44211859981 (job 134491948817). In run 44141097601 at 83ca81e709e, the test passed on Windows.\n\n## Not established\nWhy that single `hash-object --stdin-paths` call takes over 600 s on Windows:\n- per-object cost on NTFS / Defender scanning;\n- the size of the loose fill;\n- a pipe stall between the stdin writer and git.\n\nLinux and macOS finish it well under the budget.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The cost of `_fill_loose` on the Windows runner is measured: per-object time, and whether git is progressing or blocked.\n- [ ] The test finishes under the Windows sweep budget, with the cause fixed at class level and no budget raised.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"80f4-1d94-f818-4909","ticket_type":"bug","title":"bd66 maintenance test exceeds the 600 s Windows test budget inside its loose-object fill","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f3b5ddb0-36d9-428f-9312-083db789b697","ce25c9a1-5015-43a8-b149-800bbcc88250"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794978509598584906,"uuid":"9fa0ae63-0db1-40b7-a22f-2cb46cfb48d2"}
